One question has completely changed the way I approach projects.

Not...

"Can I build this?"

But...

"Should I build this?"

When I first started, I thought adding more features made a product better.

Now I spend more time removing things than adding them.

Every extra button adds a decision.

Every extra field adds friction.

Every extra feature adds complexity.

Simplicity isn't about doing less work.

It's about doing the work that matters.

The products I enjoy using the most aren't the ones with the longest list of features.

They're the ones that solve one problem really well.

That's a mindset I'm trying to carry into every project I work on.

Build less.
Solve more.

What's one feature you've seen that sounded great on paper but ended up making a product worse?

